# R13 calibration: the Rust slice's crossing benchmark, run on the PYTHON slice's machine
#
# Why this log exists: README R13. Absolutes do not travel between containers. The
# 1.8 ns crossing figure in README section 2 is a fact about the container the Rust
# slice ran in. This log is the same benchmark, same sources, on THIS machine, so that
# every absolute the python slice reports can also be quoted as a multiple of it.
#
# date:        2026-09-19T06:56:21Z
# machine:     4 vCPU, Intel(R) Xeon(R) Processor @ 2.10GHz, 15 GiB
# kernel:      6.18.44-fc-v37
# toolchain:   rustc 1.94.1 (e408947bf 2026-03-25)
# sources:     ffi/poc/rust @ d7c5a04, unmodified
# build:       cargo build --release -p harness --bin bench   (default features: guard ON)
# linkage:     libak_core.so, a cdylib, reached through the dynamic linker
# filter:      AK_BENCH_ONLY=P1.1 -- the crossing rows are retained unconditionally by
#              bench.rs, and P1.1 is kept as the cheapest in-process company for them.
#              A filtered run is as valid as a full one for the rows it keeps.

